Based on the search results, the "FSI" engine designation is primarily associated with older generations of the Audi A6 (C6, C7, around 2004-2015). The most recent generation (C8, from 2018 onwards) uses "TFSI" for petrol engines. Therefore, evaluating the *most recent* Audi A6 Saloon with an "FSI" engine is not possible as this combination does not exist in the current lineup.

Following the instructions, if data is ambiguous or unclear for a specific attribute, I must default to 0.00. This applies to all engine-specific metrics for which data for a *recent* A6 FSI is unavailable. For all other metrics, I will use the characteristics of the most recent Audi A6 Saloon (C8 generation) as established in previous evaluations.

